@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title PLANNED — Claude Code MCP launch toggle

start
:Resolve MCP mode;
if (Can this run start Claude Code
with the requested mode?) then (yes)
  if (MCP mode?) then (on)
    :Finish normal config restore;
    :Load Claude Code's current config
and add Android MCP if requested;
  else (off)
    :Pass the verified MCP disable flag
and omit Android MCP arguments;
  endif
  :Start Claude Code with the requested mode;
else (no)
  :Explain which existing session or sandbox
prevents the mode from taking effect;
  stop
endif
stop

legend bottom
  **Scope and contract**
  * Claude Code on sbx. Keep the picker precedence: environment, saved choice, then off.
  * The choice takes effect at process launch. An attached process keeps its launch settings.
  * Off skips sbx gateway setup and disables MCP in the Claude process, including the
    Android mobile server. The toggle leaves saved registrations and Android's ADB bridge intact.
  * On removes the Proveo disable flag and uses the usual Claude Code configuration discovery.
    It should see edits in the Proveo home and project configuration made between launches.
  * Gateway provisioning still uses sbx's kit lifecycle. A kept sandbox created without gateway
    hooks may need the existing carry-and-recreate flow to enable the gateway on a later run.

  **1. Verify the Claude Code flag**
  * Use the pinned Claude Code build. Check whether --strict-mcp-config alone suppresses every
    loaded server from user, project, CLI, plugin and managed sources supported by that build.
  * If the flag requires an explicit source, test an empty MCP object passed inline in argv.
    Existing Claude configuration files remain intact. Treat any bypass found here as a release blocker.

  **2. Apply the mode to the launch**
  * Build Claude Code's effective arguments once before sbx wraps them. Cover the published kit,
    image entrypoint fallback and shell fallback. Check the final argv on create and reuse.
  * Reject caller-supplied MCP arguments that conflict with off. Report the conflicting flag.
    Under on, preserve normal caller arguments and the existing Android injection behavior.
  * Keep the sbx create-time gateway gate. If sbx can only attach to an already-running process
    whose mode differs or cannot be verified, stop and explain the restart required.
    Use the existing confirmation flow before any replacement that would end a kept session.

  **3. Restore current config before an on launch**
  * Fresh sandboxes stage the declared home-root files and restore config before launch.
  * Reused sandboxes keep the mounts they were created with. Refresh the declared files in
    the home-files directory the sandbox actually uses, then restore via the existing sync
    path before starting Claude. Reuse the existing locking and newer-wins rules.
  * If the recorded mount cannot be refreshed safely, use the existing sandbox replacement
    flow or report the failure. Respect PROVEO_CONFIG_SYNC and the declared config paths.

  **4. Verify the round trip**
  |= Area |= Acceptance check |
  | Run and posture | Defaults, remembered choice and env override. Explain MCP versus the sbx gateway. |
  | Backend and sbx | Off argv survives launch wrappers and reattach. Android MCP and conflicting CLI options cannot bypass it. ADB remains available. |
  | Config sync | Existing entries survive off. Reuse an on sandbox after a host edit that adds one server and removes another. Verify both changes reach Claude Code. |
  | Live sbx | Start on with a gateway and a project server, then launch off with Android selected. Inspect /mcp in that session and assert zero servers. Edit the saved config, return to on and verify the new server answers. |
  | Kept sessions | A running on process cannot be reattached and reported as off. Apply the change after explicit restart. |
  | Static checks | Run go vet on touched packages and validate this diagram. |
endlegend
@enduml
